WEBVTT

00:00:00.063 --> 00:00:05.340
A drone program may manage still imagery, video, thermal files, telemetry, flight logs,

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:08.620
maps, models, inspection notes, annotations, and reports.

00:00:08.620 --> 00:00:11.800
Every product should remain linked to the mission, aircraft, sensor, time,

00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:14.395
location confidence, and responsible reviewer.

00:00:14.395 --> 00:00:18.830
Use consistent file names, mission identifiers, folder structures, and metadata rules.

00:00:18.830 --> 00:00:21.401
Preserve originals separately from processed outputs.

00:00:21.401 --> 00:00:26.160
Record transformations such as stitching, enhancement, redaction, annotation, conversion,

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:28.123
or artificial-intelligence assistance.

00:00:28.123 --> 00:00:32.645
Storage design addresses capacity, performance, encryption, backup, recovery, retention,

00:00:32.645 --> 00:00:34.395
legal hold, and deletion.

00:00:34.395 --> 00:00:38.140
Exports and temporary working copies deserve the same protection as the central repository

00:00:38.140 --> 00:00:40.488
because they may contain equivalent sensitive data.

00:00:40.488 --> 00:00:45.200
G I S integration can connect observations to authorized maps and asset records.

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:48.210
Position metadata should be validated when navigation anomalies occur.

00:00:48.210 --> 00:00:51.615
Dashboards should communicate coverage, status, findings, confidence,

00:00:51.615 --> 00:00:53.873
and gaps without overstating precision.

00:00:53.873 --> 00:00:58.060
Reporting workflows distinguish direct observation, automated output, analyst judgment,

00:00:58.060 --> 00:00:59.800
and specialist diagnosis.

00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:03.470
Quality review should check evidence references, privacy, accuracy, uncertainty,

00:01:03.470 --> 00:01:06.000
and whether the product answers the mission request.

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:10.430
Protect sensitive imagery of people, property, facilities, infrastructure, and operations.

00:01:10.430 --> 00:01:14.120
Limit distribution to legitimate recipients, control public release,

00:01:14.120 --> 00:01:18.280
and retain only what policy, law, evidence, and operational need justify.

00:01:18.280 --> 00:01:21.504
Where evidence integrity matters, preserve collection and processing lineage:

00:01:21.504 --> 00:01:25.560
who captured, transferred, transformed, reviewed, approved, and exported each product.

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:29.300
This supports correction and accountability without claiming that every operational image

00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:30.400
is forensic evidence.
